Three robustness fixes to SimArt's inference entry point, applied in-tree.

1. `attn_implementation` was hardcoded to "flash_attention_2". Building
   flash_attn from source needs an exact torch/CPython/CUDA match and ~30 min,
   so an entire pipeline run should not hinge on that wheel resolving. It is
   now an env var defaulting to "sdpa"; set SIMART_ATTN_IMPL=flash_attention_2
   to restore the original behaviour.

2. `json.loads(response.strip())` was unguarded, on up to 24k tokens of model
   output, and ran AFTER generation had already been paid for. Stray prose or a
   truncated response crashed with a bare JSONDecodeError and nothing to
   inspect. The raw response is now written to disk and named in the error.

3. The checkpoint samples (do_sample=true, temperature=0.7) and infer.py never
   seeds, so identical inputs give different articulations run to run.
   SIMART_SEED=<int> pins the sampler (offset per object in folder runs);
   unset keeps upstream's non-deterministic behaviour.

Apply/revert from the SimArt checkout:
    git -C ../SimArt apply      ../pipeline/patches/simart_infer.patch
    git -C ../SimArt apply -R   ../pipeline/patches/simart_infer.patch
Check first with `git apply --check` -- it is a no-op if already applied.

diff --git a/inference/infer.py b/inference/infer.py
index 7399966..874445c 100644
--- a/inference/infer.py
+++ b/inference/infer.py
@@ -287,8 +287,13 @@ def main():
